% ============================================================================
% quadrilateral-alt-name.query.adj — a worked recall over the geometry
% quadrilateral-alt-name library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what's another word
% for a rhombus?": it states no geometry fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine
% resolves each `?` against the `quadrilateral_alt_name` rows and returns
% the alternate name + the table's source/locator/trust. A shape the cited
% spans give no alternate name for abstains honestly — the engine never
% invents one.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli quadrilateral-alt-name.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "quadrilateral-alt-name.adj"

? quadrilateral_alt_name(rhombus, $AltName)                           % expect equilateral_parallelogram
? quadrilateral_alt_name($Shape, equilateral_parallelogram)           % reverse bind — expect rhombus
? quadrilateral_alt_name(square, $AltName)                            % expect abstain — square's own cited span names no alternate word
